        ("sales-proposal", "Customer Proposal", "Draft a customer proposal tied to stated needs, outcomes, scope, assumptions, and evidence.", "Use confirmed requirements, measurable outcomes, deliverables, exclusions, timeline assumptions, responsibilities, pricing source, and acceptance. Flag unsupported claims and route commercial or legal terms for approval."),
        ("sales-negotiation", "Commercial Negotiation Preparation", "Prepare negotiation options and concession boundaries grounded in approved commercial policy.", "Identify customer priorities, our walk-away conditions, value exchange, approval limits, and conditional concessions. Never invent authority, promise unapproved terms, or misrepresent alternatives."),
        ("sales-objection", "Customer Objection Response", "Answer a sales objection with accurate evidence and a useful next question.", "Clarify the concern, respond only with verified product or service evidence, acknowledge limits, and ask what would resolve the issue. Escalate roadmap, security, legal, or performance claims to an owner."),
        ("sales-territory", "Territory and Coverage Plan", "Balance account coverage and sales capacity across a territory using transparent criteria.", "Use account potential evidence, segment, workload, geography, existing commitments, and representative capacity. Show assumptions and fairness checks; do not treat proxy data as certain buying intent."),
        ("sales-renewal", "Renewal and Expansion Plan", "Protect a renewal by connecting adoption, realized outcomes, risks, and agreed next value.", "Review usage and outcomes against the customer plan, open issues, stakeholders, renewal dates, and contract facts. Identify at-risk gaps honestly and agree an actionable recovery or expansion path."),
